Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)#{1}":[30,31],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/38JF7P4G","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=2&annotation=RJ2VDYFU","line":30},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=1&annotation=2VKJYJXQ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=3&annotation=3XESQ9KG","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=4&annotation=B64P7DLW","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=4&annotation=E8L5NPSP","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 8","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=8&annotation=KRP5TGUI","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 11","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=11&annotation=5B993LQJ","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 11","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=11&annotation=DWFPZ53X","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 8","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=8&annotation=GK8JNWFG","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 8","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XBRAQY77?page=8&annotation=IPLIVBPH","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols Diet: A Novel Approach for the Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome","Authors":"Varol Tunali, Naciye Çiğdem Arslan, Beyza Hilal Ermiş, Gözde Derviş Hakim, Aycan Gündoğdu, Mehmet Hora, Özkan Ufuk Nalbantoğlu","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.14309/ajg.0000000000002862","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This multicenter randomized controlled trial focuses on comparing the efficacy of a microbiome-based artificial intelligence-assisted personalized diet (PD) with a low-fermentable oligosaccharides, disaccharides, monosaccharides, and polyols diet (FODMAP) for IBS management.The Enbiosis personalized nutrition model (ENBIOSIS Biotechnologies, London, UK), which is based on machine learning models to evaluate the microbiome and recommend conditioned nutritional actions (14), is used to determine the ideal micronutriencompositions for modulating the microbiome. In this study, the model calculated the required microbiome modulation for an individual by analyzing the IBS indices generated by machine learning modelThe algorithm recommended daily diets based on the nutritional compositions suggested by the model. Thus, the algorithm evaluated the IBS index score using the microbiome composition to design optimized diets that aim to modulate the microbiome toward healthier scores.This study aimed to investigate the effects of 2 dietary interventions, namely the microbiome-based AI-assisted PD and the FODMAP diet, on individuals with IBS across different subtypes, as classified by the Rome IV criteria.","Findings":"","Conclusions":"Our findings contribute to a comprehensive understanding of the potential benefits of personalized dietary interventions tailored to specific IBS subtypThese findings support the potential of a personalized dietary approach to not only alleviate symptoms but also enhance the overall QOL for individuals with IBS.In conclusion, our study provides evidence supporting the effectiveness of a tailor-made PD, such as the PD, for managing IBS symptoms and improving QOL across different subtypes.  While the FODMAP diet remains the standard dietary approach for symptom relief in many clinical settings, our findings suggest that considering individual patient characteristics, including the IBS subtype, may further optimize treatment outcomes and by achieving a healthier microbiome status, the overall health status of patients with IBS may be improved.3 Microbiome-based artificial intelligence-assisted personalized diets (PDs) show promise for IBS management.  3 PD demonstrates effectiveness in reducing symptoms of IBS across all subtypes.  3 PD intervention leads to significant microbiome diversity shift","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"18xn4qy","at":1769791540537}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian/A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial of Microbiome-Based Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Personalized Diet vs Low-Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyol.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06863921,-0.02618947,0.03640178,-0.00883036,0.00502445,-0.01605935,-0.03295906,0.05111234,0.00209794,-0.03464823,0.03518567,-0.14796574,0.01681869,0.02238853,0.05297157,-0.00285635,0.02434397,0.02243692,-0.04891653,-0.00952537,0.08625164,-0.06165143,-0.00021225,0.00133952,0.01075759,0.03956741,0.02252449,-0.03231838,-0.08491606,-0.24476188,0.03074269,-0.03747164,0.1064865,-0.03196838,-0.07520364,-0.00393629,-0.03745156,0.04816665,-0.07247028,0.05188151,0.03934551,0.01440303,0.01397785,0.00669211,0.02933001,-0.0405965,-0.02921709,-0.02919856,-0.03654078,-0.0290325,0.00355497,-0.04353773,-0.01123054,0.02736333,0.03731377,0.02819278,-0.00438761,0.01472919,0.03491306,0.05199001,0.03740185,0.0719769,-0.18665512,0.08940629,0.04027021,0.01571224,-0.03178333,-0.00936154,0.02958436,-0.02786389,-0.05934738,0.03759433,0.0532997,0.04781376,0.00657339,0.0036181,0.05829027,-0.03894915,0.0270374,0.04204413,-0.02196404,0.07907557,-0.02682201,-0.01376843,-0.06667595,-0.01232674,-0.00321096,-0.0948289,0.06198